## Educational Applications

The simulator provides an educational platform for studying and demonstrating technologies related to biomedical engineering, including:

- Surgical robotics and biomechatronic systems.
- Robotic kinematics and motion control.
- Three-dimensional modeling and virtual simulation.
- Software development and automation.
- Remote control and communication systems.
- Medical image acquisition and processing.
- DICOM standards and PACS technologies.
- Artificial intelligence applications in biomedical systems.
- Integration of multidisciplinary engineering technologies.

## Project Results

The project resulted in the development of a **functional educational robotic surgery simulation prototype** that integrates mechanical simulation, remote control, virtual visualization, medical image processing, PACS storage, and experimental artificial intelligence.

The system demonstrates how different biomedical engineering technologies can be integrated into a single interactive platform for educational, research, and technological demonstration purposes.

## Disclaimer

This project was developed exclusively for **academic, educational, and experimental research purposes**.

It is not an official MAKO surgical system, is not clinically certified, and is not intended for real surgical procedures, medical diagnosis, or clinical decision-making.

MAKO is a trademark associated with Stryker. This educational project is not affiliated with or endorsed by Stryker.
